      "message": "Removing this PF3 stylesheet results in some texts being much larger than before. I noticed this in the \"console-like\" output that is shown in the Task Summary and Console tabs on the build result page. It looks like the PF3 stylesheet reduced the font-size for \u003cpre\u003e tags from the 16px (PF4 default) to 11px. I don\u0027t have a strong opinion on this, but since we are used to the smaller font-size it might make sense to add some rules to our custom CSS stylesheet to keep those smaller font-sizes although PF4 would use larger fonts by default.\n\nThe same applies to all tables (there the font-size changed from 12px to 16px).\n\nI\u0027ve also noticed some other differences\n- Status page (PipelineOverview): Some fonts look bold that weren\u0027t bold before and vice-versa (I think we can live with it as you can only spot the difference in direct comparison to the old UI).\n- Status page (PipelineOverview): The spaces between the QueueItem boxes are gone\n- General: Headings (h1, h2, h3) don\u0027t have a margin anymore (previously: margin-bottom: 10px, margin-top: 20px).\n- Menu bar: The spaces between the different menu items are gone. This results e.g. in the config-error alert bell being squashed into the timezone selector.\n\nI find that some of those issues make the UI look a bit broken, so I think we should attract those first - especially the larger font-sizes and the missing spaces. It might be enough to add some CSS rules to our custom CSS stylesheet.",
